1. create django project >> django-admin startproject <NAME>

2. create django app >> py manage.py startapp <NAME>

3. set up geodjango
    setting.py > add 'django.contrib.gis'
    install GDAL / osgeo4w
    add  C:\OSGeo4W\bin sa System PATH
    run: dir C:\OSGeo4W\bin\gdal*.dll (to get version) and dir C:\OSGeo4W\bin\geos_c*.dll
    add the geodjango setting code in setting.py

4. set up postgis
    settings.py under databases, change the value
        'default': {
            'ENGINE': 'django.contrib.gis.db.backends.postgis',
            'NAME':'ph_ch_project',
            'USER': 'postgres',
            'PASSWORD': 'postgres',
            'HOST': 'localhost',
            'PORT': '5432'
        }
    pip install psycopg2

5. link apps created to geodjango project
    in settings.py under installed_apps, link apps
        app > apps.py > <ch_backend.apps.ChBackendConfig>

6. run python manage.py migrate

7. start creating super user <py manage.py createsuperuser> <admin:admin>

### MODELS

8. Create models
    import the geodjango models > from django.contrib.gis.db import models
    set up media folder when using an image field in your models
        add to settings.py >    MEDIA_ROOT = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, 'media')
                                MEDIA_URL = '/media/'
    
    do migrations for both app models and database
        py manage.py makemigrations <appname>
        py manage.py migrate

9. Register you models in admin.py
    make sure to use contrib.gis < from django.contrib.gis import admin
    create custom geodAdmin for models using geo attributes


### MEDIA
10. for media, link the media files to ph_ch_project URL 
        from django.conf import settings
        from django.conf.urls.static import static

        + static(settings.MEDIA_URL, document_root=settings.MEDIA_ROOT)

11. install 3rd party app to ensure when deleting an item, the media files will also be deleted
    > pip install django-cleanup
    in settings.py add the app > 'django_cleanup.apps.CleanupConfig',


### VIEWS

12. Create a urls.py in your app folder to link your views. This will be your sub-urls 
    in urls.py add 
        > from django.urls import path, 
    then create your patterns url for your views
        > from . import views 

13. Link your sub urls to your main urls in project folder
        import another package > from django.urls import include
        add to patterns_url > path('', include('<APPNAME>.urls'))


   
    